{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_obstruction_link","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_obstruction_link","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qou_obstruction_reduction"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qcollatz_kummer_removable_of_chi_neg_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qcollatz_kummer_removable_of_chi_neg_six","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_obstruction_link.lean#L44-L52","doc":"**Descartes instance.** In a Descartes universe `χ(A) = −6`, so `2 ∣ χ(A)` and\nthe q-Collatz even-branch `[2]_q` obstruction vanishes — the Kummer divisor is\nremovable. Stated with `χ(A) = −6` as an explicit hypothesis, since that value\nis Descartes-specific, not general-QOU. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qcollatz_kummer_removable_iff_two_dvd_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qcollatz_kummer_removable_iff_two_dvd_chi","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_obstruction_link.lean#L35-L42","doc":"**C9 — q-Collatz even-branch Kummer removability ⟺ `2 ∣ χ(A)`.** Conditional\non the universal obstruction context, the level-2 residue `κ_C` of the `χ(A)`\nclass vanishes — the q-Collatz `[2]_q` divisor is removable — iff `2 ∣ χ(A)`.\nThe q-Collatz specialisation (`n = 2`) of `kappa_vanishes_iff_chi`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}